 is pretty cool it's a  bucky talking to sam and he says the  people need something to get behind  and it's probably a very emotional time  for him because that's who his best  friend  steve rogers the old captain america was  he was a symbol to the people  and during a time of uncertainty after  avengers in-game and during a time where  there's a bunch of terrorist attacks it  seems  the people are definitely going to need  somebody to get behind and it looks like  bucky is encouraging sam to be that  person to be that symbol of hope  we then get our first official look at  falcon  suit it's kind of blurry in the scene  but we can see the new design  and it doesn't seem like he's taken on  the mantle at this point of captain  america but if we take a look at this  next clip of sam  shaking his head he looks rather  emotional as he's doing this  and this is no doubt sam's nodding and  agreeing with bucky  when he said that the people need  something to get behind we then have a  scene where they very clearly show baron  zemo  in this scene we see zemo grieving his  family but perhaps he's not as vengeful  as he was before  as we know and as we've seen in this  trailer he will be working with sam and  bucky and of course we've seen this shot  before which is bucky's arm  dropping bullets in front of zemo which  is a scene that we're kind of unsure  about right now but many people believe  it to be  bucky letting go dropping the bullets  not killing zemo but forgiving him  we then see the new captain america not  sam but u.s  agent john walker running on the  football field now as he runs on the  field and they show the new captain  america symbol we hear bucky's words  they need a symbol talking about the  people now this implies what we kind of  knew all along us agent john walker  isn't exactly the best person and has  ulterior motives of being captain  america whether he's being brainwashed  by somebody like thunderbolt ross or  perhaps even hydra  or perhaps he's even doing it on his own  we know that he's not going  to remain captain america because he's  going to be a little bit corrupt which  is why bucky says that sam  needs to be that symbol we then see the  falcon and the winter soldier in  action sam of course is flying and doing  some pretty awesome stunts but bucky now  has a motorcycle  and this might be bucky's thing in the  series the falcon can fly he has his  wings and bucky may have a motorcycle  most of the time to keep up which is  pretty awesome and hopefully makes for  some really awesome scenes  we again run into the flag smashers but  specifically the same girl from before  we then have a bunch of more action  sequences but then we get this really  awesome clip of sam kicking this woman  just  like captain america steve rogers used  to kick people so there's definitely  going to be a lot of callbacks to chris  evans as steve rogers  now all throughout this trailer it looks  like the flag smashers are the ones  responsible for these terrorist attacks  and this heist  and throughout the trailer sam and bucky  are trying to stop them but in the scene  where we have sam and bucky in a plane  and bucky asks what the plan is and  there is no plan according to sam  because he just jumps out the plane  but we can see that there is a u.s  soldier on board  so at one point in time it looks like  they're going to have the backing of the  us army on their side  either that or a lot of people are still  very loyal to captain america so they  want to help out sam and bucky  but in a time of terror it would make  sense that the government would hire two  avengers who helped the world in  avengers infinity war and avengers  in-game  despite their past we then cut to an  amazing scene with a helicopter chasing  sam  firing at him and sam maneuvering his  way through canyons avoiding getting hit  by these missiles and it looks  absolutely fantastic super action-packed  and if this is a preview of what the  show is going 